## Responsive Design

### Breakpoint Strategy

Follow Tailwind's default breakpoints:
- `sm`: 640px (large phones)
- `md`: 768px (tablets)
- `lg`: 1024px (laptops)
- `xl`: 1280px (desktops)
- `2xl`: 1536px (large desktops)

### Mobile-First Principles

1. **Start with mobile layout**, then add complexity at larger breakpoints
2. **Stack elements vertically** on mobile, arrange horizontally on larger screens
3. **Reduce spacing** on mobile (e.g., `py-12` → `py-8`)
4. **Simplify navigation** to hamburger menu on mobile
5. **Full-width buttons** on mobile, inline on desktop

### Responsive Patterns

```jsx
// Typography scaling
<h1 className="
  text-3xl      /* mobile */
  sm:text-4xl   /* tablet */
  md:text-5xl   /* small laptop */
  lg:text-6xl   /* laptop */
  xl:text-7xl   /* desktop */
">

// Grid changes
<div className="
  grid 
  grid-cols-1       /* mobile: single column */
  sm:grid-cols-2    /* tablet: two columns */
  lg:grid-cols-3    /* laptop: three columns */
  gap-4 md:gap-6 lg:gap-8
">

// Section padding
<section className="
  py-12        /* mobile */
  md:py-16     /* tablet */
  lg:py-24     /* laptop */
  xl:py-32     /* desktop */
">

// Flex direction
<div className="
  flex 
  flex-col     /* mobile: stack */
  md:flex-row  /* tablet+: horizontal */
  gap-4
">

// Hide/show elements
<div className="hidden md:block">  {/* Show only on md+ */}
<div className="md:hidden">         {/* Show only below md */}
```

