## Do's and Don'ts

### ✅ Do

- **Use the brand colors consistently** — stick to the defined palette
- **Maintain generous whitespace** — let content breathe
- **Use serif (Erstoria) for headlines** — it builds trust and warmth
- **Apply subtle animations** — enhance without distracting
- **Keep CTAs clear and prominent** — one primary action per section
- **Use real photography when possible** — avoid generic stock
- **Test at all breakpoints** — ensure responsive excellence
- **Follow the component patterns** — maintain consistency
- **Use the correct font weights** — semibold for headings, regular for body

### ❌ Don't

- **Don't introduce new colors** — stay within the brand palette
- **Don't use pure black (#000)** — use deep teal (#2f3e46) instead
- **Don't use flashy animations** — keep motion subtle and purposeful
- **Don't mix multiple serif fonts** — stick to Erstoria
- **Don't clutter layouts** — embrace minimalism
- **Don't use thin font weights** — maintain readability
- **Don't skip focus states** — accessibility is mandatory
- **Don't use generic stock photos** — curate imagery carefully
- **Don't overuse the sage accent** — it's for highlights, not dominance
- **Don't forget mobile** — design mobile-first
- **Don't use bouncy/playful animations** — maintain professionalism
- **Don't add drop shadows to everything** — use shadows purposefully

