## Shared Component Library

### Component Inventory

These reusable components live in `src/components/shared/` and follow the [Component Architecture](./COMPONENT_ARCHITECTURE.md) rules.

| Component | File | Purpose | Key Props |
|-----------|------|---------|-----------|
| **Breadcrumbs** | `breadcrumbs.tsx` | Auto-generated breadcrumbs from pathname | `className?`, `items?` (override) |
| **DirectoryBreadcrumbs** | `directory-breadcrumbs.tsx` | Public directory page navigation | `items`, `className?` |
| **EditSlugDialog** | `edit-slug-dialog.tsx` | URL slug editor with validation | `currentSlug`, `entityType`, `onSave` |
| **EmptyState** | `empty-state.tsx` | Animated empty state with actions | `iconName`, `title`, `description`, `actions?`, `compact?`, `animated?` |
| **EmptyStateCard** | `empty-state.tsx` | Compact variant for smaller spaces | Same as EmptyState |
| **WelcomeBanner** | `empty-state.tsx` | Onboarding welcome with step tracker | `steps`, `completedSteps` |
| **ImageUpload** | `image-upload.tsx` | Dropzone + crop + upload | `variant` (logo/avatar/banner/profile-photo), `onUpload`, `currentUrl?` |
| **StatCard** | `stat-card.tsx` | Metric card with trend indicator | `title`, `value`, `icon?`, `change?`, `isLoading?` |
| **StatCardGrid** | `stat-card.tsx` | Responsive grid wrapper for StatCards | `children`, `columns` (2-6) |
| **StatusBadge** | `status-badge.tsx` | Config-driven status display | `status`, `config` |
| **TierBadge** | `tier-badge.tsx` | Gamification tier (Enterprise/Pro) | `isEnterprise`, `isPro`, `size?` |
| **TierBadgeSSR** | `tier-badge-ssr.tsx` | SSR-safe variant (no tooltips) | Same as TierBadge |
| **ReviewItem** | `review-item.tsx` | Review card with rating, share, flag | `review`, `shareConfig?`, `onFlag?`, `animate?` |
| **Skeletons** | `skeletons.tsx` | Loading placeholders (10 types) | Varies per skeleton type |
| **CsvImportWizard** | `csv-import-wizard/` | 4-step CSV import flow | Complex multi-step props |

### Shared Component API Rules

All shared components **must**:
1. Accept `className?: string` for composition
2. Never import server actions (use callback props)
3. Export props interface as `{ComponentName}Props`
4. Use `"use client"` only when genuinely needed
5. Avoid hardcoded copy (use props with defaults)

