### Card Header Variants

`CardHeader` supports a `variant` prop for consistent visual separation across contexts:

| Variant | Styles | When to use |
|---------|--------|-------------|
| `"default"` | Sage gradient bg + border-bottom + rounded-t-xl | Dashboard cards (most cards) — **this is the default** |
| `"plain"` | No bg, no border (original behavior) | Auth, onboarding, public, marketing pages |
| `"accent-amber"` | Amber gradient + amber border-bottom | Warning/destructive contexts (e.g. account deactivation) |
| `"accent-green"` | Green gradient + green border-bottom | Success/action contexts (e.g. smart actions) |

```tsx
// Dashboard card — default variant, no prop needed
<CardHeader>
  <CardTitle>Dashboard Card</CardTitle>
</CardHeader>

// Auth/public page — plain variant
<CardHeader variant="plain">
  <CardTitle>Login</CardTitle>
</CardHeader>

// Warning context
<CardHeader variant="accent-amber">
  <CardTitle>Deactivate Account</CardTitle>
</CardHeader>
```

**Rule:** All dashboard cards use the default variant (no prop needed). Non-dashboard contexts (auth, onboarding, public profiles, marketing) must use `variant="plain"`.

